            <div xml:id="d348">

                <pb facs="0518" n="204" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg204"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/1334</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reinsch</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1914-12-23T14:00:00+08:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">December 23, 1914, 2 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Referring to my cable of December 18, 7 p.m., Japanese now demand appointment to
                    Tsingtao customs of forty-nine officials taken from Japanese customs
                    administration. This affects the treaty powers as such action would break up the
                    organization of Maritime Customs Service.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
